{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Report\n\nMultiple concurrent sessions simultaneously report `rebar review-plan` returning **INDETERMINATE** (unsigned, no determinate PASS/FAIL verdict). Sudden fleet-wide onset during a period of heavy concurrent multi-worktree activity (~70 worktrees; multiple sessions + a fanned-out batch of debug agents each running review-plan).\n\n## Observed (descriptive; not yet root-caused)\n\n- INDETERMINATE affects MULTIPLE independent sessions at once (systemic, not per-ticket).\n- Local host resources are HEALTHY: load avg ~3.5, disk 28% used (1.3Ti free), no orphaned/leaked busy-loops (scripts/check_orphaned_load.py clean bar system daemons). So NOT local CPU/disk/leak exhaustion on this box.\n- Provider config: rebar DEFAULTS TO AWS BEDROCK (`[llm] model = bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8`, acct 896586841071/us-east-1; rebar.toml ~L145-222). Config explicitly states the chain does NOT fail over on a credential error ('a credential error must not be masked by shopping for a provider whose key happens to work'). frontier class (review-plan) = opus on Bedrock; mixed-provider chains disable prompt caching.\n- Tickets branch shows three-way divergence at report time (local cb530119, remote-tracking af98dfad, actual origin/tickets 4fbe6114) — heavy concurrent ticket writes from many sessions.\n\n## Leads to test (for the investigator — do NOT confirm from source alone; these are dynamic)\n\n1. **Bedrock account-level throttling** (ThrottlingException / 429 / TPM/RPM quota) from a burst of concurrent frontier/opus review-plan runs across sessions sharing ONE Bedrock account, mis-surfaced as INDETERMINATE with no failover. Likely SELF-INFLICTED by concurrent fan-out. Check the runner's exception classification (src/rebar/llm/runner.py, structured_run.py, review_kernel/verify.py+decide.py) for how a provider throttle/timeout/truncation degrades to INDETERMINATE.\n2. **Stale-store gate refusal** — recent main commit 'Refuse gate certification on a stale store' (2598909d) + 'Fail closed on an unobtainable claim-gate basis' (1c0a202b). Under concurrent tickets-branch write contention the store could read stale for many sessions at once, refusing certification → INDETERMINATE. Check whether a stale-store refusal path returns INDETERMINATE.\n3. Truncation/length collapse (structured_run.py:522 'finish_reason=length ... collapses to INDETERMINATE') under a degraded/throttled provider returning partial turns.\n\n## Impact\n\nFleet-wide: no session can pass the plan-review claim gate → cannot claim tickets → work stalls across all sessions. Agents cannot --force (disallowed).\n\n## Investigate WITHOUT adding Bedrock load\n\nDo NOT reproduce by running live review-plan storms against Bedrock — that aggravates the incident. Reproduce the CLASSIFICATION path with an injected/mocked provider throttle/timeout/truncation and assert the resulting verdict, and inspect the stale-store refusal path locally.\n\nReported against origin/main at commit 55589c15 (current HEAD at report time).\n\n---\n\n## Fix plan (Phase 2 — Direction C.c1, operator-approved)\n\n**Change:** in `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py`, `should_fall_back`, EXCLUDE the `WAIT_AND_RETRY`\ndisposition from the cross-provider failover predicate. Today it returns True for\n`resolution_class in _RETRYABLE ({WAIT_AND_RETRY, RETRY_NOW}) or CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL`;\nchange it to return True only for `RETRY_NOW or CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL`. A plain Bedrock 429\naccount-throttle (`WAIT_AND_RETRY`) then RETRIES THE PRIMARY (Bedrock adaptive backoff, exit-11\nretryable) instead of failing the frontier chain over to a keyless `anthropic:opus` whose\nterminal auth error masks the retryable primary cause as a hard INDETERMINATE.\n\nThis restores the pre-`8fbd` retryable-throttle disposition and EXTENDS the invariant already\ndocumented in `rebar.toml` (~L197) — \"a credential error must not be masked by shopping for a\nprovider whose key happens to work\" — to the throttle case. `RETRY_NOW` (a down local endpoint,\nthe case cross-provider failover genuinely exists for) and `CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL` STILL fail\nover. `_RETRYABLE` in `failure.py` is UNCHANGED — a throttle stays exit-11 retryable, it just no\nlonger fails over.\n\n**Scope:** `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py` (the predicate + its docstring/import) and\n`tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py` (a new RED oracle asserting a throttle does not fail\nover, plus updating the pre-existing tests that encoded the old WAIT_AND_RETRY→failover\ncontract). No change to `failure.py` or `rebar.toml`.\n\n**Attribution:** caused_by `8fbd-e9d5-326e-40d8` (commit `6d4f394195b2`, \"Enable class-scoped\nAnthropic fallback\", 2026-08-10), class `plan_defect` — its plan enabled cross-provider failover\non a retryable throttle without a credential-reachable-fallback guard. Fix site\n(`should_fall_back`) is not the cause site (8fbd's config plan).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. `should_fall_back` returns **False** for a `WAIT_AND_RETRY` failure (a plain 429 rate-limit /\n   529 overloaded / read-timeout) — no cross-provider failover.\n2. `should_fall_back` STILL returns **True** for `RETRY_NOW` and `CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL`, and\n   STILL **False** for `CHANGE_SETTINGS` (credential/quota) and `NEEDS_INVESTIGATION`.\n3. End-to-end (mocked provider, NO real Bedrock): a throttled primary in the frontier\n   `FallbackModel` chain no longer fails over to the keyless anthropic fallback; the throttle\n   surfaces as the exit-11 **retryable** disposition, NOT INDETERMINATE.\n4. A RED oracle proves criterion 1/3 fails before the change and passes after; a mutation\n   (re-introducing `WAIT_AND_RETRY` into the failover set) is caught (RED).\n5. `make lint` + `make typecheck` clean; no new dependency; no test weakening."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788047753066239029,"uuid":"c7c71447-8e17-4e2c-ac43-0dd63aefe33c"}